      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 137, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced course catalog table: an alternative catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags, section flags, meeting time/place), plus subject-offering reference columns (SO_SUBJECT_ID, SO_TERM_CODE, SO_TERM_DESCRIPTION, SO_CLUSTER_TYPE) linking catalog records to registrar subject offerings.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLABLE\", \"desc\": \"11 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Library reserve material detail bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, course instructors, and material status per term. Used to count reserved materials per subject and to filter by library material status (e.g. 'U').\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\", \"desc\": \"Library course instructor table recording instructors of courses with library reserve materials, including course name, instructor name, department (in 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' format), assignment date range, and library organizational unit/branch. Referenced by LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY; instructor names resolve to person records via INSTRUCTOR_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject category lookup table with category name and description. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"Subject attribute lookup table decoding attribute codes attached to subjects: academic attributes (type 'A') such as calculus/science prerequisites and HASS-D/HASS category codes, and non-academic program flags (type 'N') such as ROTC, ESG, Concourse, co-op, and listener rules. Provides short, full, and reporting descriptions per code. Overlaps with CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE on HASS-family codes (HD1-HD5, HDL, HE, HA, HH, HS) but differs in scope: SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE covers all subject attribute types with one description variant per code, while CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE covers only HASS attribute codes with separate registration-form and bulletin descriptions plus attribute-group (H/G) classification. Catalog subject records' GIR_ATTRIBUTE codes all resolve against SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"desc\": \"TIP material status lookup table decoding material status keys/codes used in TIP_DETAIL. Holds 12 status rows where key and code are identical: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and four keys ('NL', 'NS', 'NB', and a blank/space key) that share a NULL description.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEGREE_PROGRAM\", \"desc\": \"19 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Independent Activities Period (IAP) subject detail table: one row per IAP activity offered in a January term, with activity title/description, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, fee, prerequisites, preregistration deadline, cancellation and multiple-session flags, and foreign keys to category, sponsor, session, and person tables.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"desc\": \"Library material status lookup table decoding library material status keys/codes used in LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL. Holds six statuses where key and code are identical: 'U' = Unknown, 'R' = (null description), 'N' = Non-Required Course Material, 'O' = Reserve only, 'X' = No Required Textbook, 'Y' = Required Course Material.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_MATERIAL\", \"desc\": \"TIP material dimension table describing textbook materials: title, author, edition, publisher, year, ISBN, new/used shelf prices and rental prices, and information source. Referenced by TIP_DETAIL via TIP_MATERIAL_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SELECTOR\", \"desc\": \"16 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_IAP_SCHEDULE\", \"desc\": \"10 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject person table: one row per person associated with an IAP activity, recording the person's role in the activity (Activity leader, Session leader, Contact person), MIT affiliation type, name, location, email, organization, and title. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON_KEY; used to analyze activity leadership and person roles, e.g. enrollment capacity statistics per person role.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"CIS lookup table decoding HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute codes used in course catalog subject records. Each code (e.g. 'HA', 'HH', 'HS', 'HE', 'HD1'-'HD5', 'HDL', and combined codes like 'HA,HH') maps to two description variants: the description shown on the registration form and the shorter description printed in the bulletin, plus the CIS attribute group ('H' = HASS_ATTRIBUTE for students entering Fall 2010 or later, 'G' = GIR_ATTRIBUTE for students entering prior to Fall 2010) with a group note, and icon display attributes. Catalog tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG) join to this lookup via HASS_ATTRIBUTE. Note: a code can appear once per attribute group (e.g. 'HE' exists in both group H and group G), so joins on HASS_ATTRIBUTE alone may produce multiple matching rows.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SESSION\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject session table: session-level details of IAP activities including session title, description, location, date, start/end times, and sequence. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SESSION_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject sponsor table listing sponsors of IAP activities with sponsor name and type. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_FACULTY_ROSTER\", \"desc\": \"HR faculty roster table: one row per faculty member keyed by MIT_ID with name components, terminal degree, appointment type, job/position titles across HR, administrative, and directory organization units, endowed chair, and emeritus status. Used for faculty appointment and credential analysis; joins to EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MIT_ID for contact details.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_GROUPING\", \"desc\": \"7 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"OPA_PERSON_CURRENT\", \"desc\": \"Current-person snapshot table from the OPA (Office of People Analytics) feed: one row per current person keyed by MIT_ID with name components, email, HR job attributes (job id/title, admin employee type, HR department, org unit and position titles, payroll rank), faculty flag, employment percent, privacy flags, sabbatical begin/end dates, and personnel subarea. Used for HR/appointment analysis of current people; carries no office phone or office location.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\", \"desc\": \"Department parent lookup table: one row per department code (D_CODE) with its department name and the identity of its direct parent department (parent ID, parent D code, parent name). A flattened single-level parent view of the department tree; use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY when the full multi-level hierarchy path of a DLC is required. D_CODE matches MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE and other DLC key columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\", \"desc\": \"Term parameter reference table holding exactly three rows that identify the SIS current term, previous term, and upcoming term, each with its term code, description, start/end dates and the last day before the next term. Used to resolve relative term references ('C', 'P', 'F') to concrete term codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_HOLIDAY_CLOSING_CALENDAR\", \"desc\": \"4 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIP\", \"desc\": \"Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) lookup table: one row per six-digit CIP program code, classifying instructional programs into a two-digit category and a four-digit series, with program/category/four-digit titles, a change note, the CIP revision version year (1990/2000/2010/2020), and the warehouse load date. Joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs, categories, and schools/departments; CIP_WITH_VERSION is the multi-version variant keeping every revision of each program code.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4602\", \"desc\": \"Show the department full names, subject titles, total units, and the number of unique course materials per subject for subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering. For each subject, also provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key, where the subject title and department code match between the subject and course material datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3668\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject title, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Additionally, for each matching course material detail, provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, the course number description, the offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key. The results should include the subject title, total units, department full name, window row number, material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students, in that order, for subjects and course materials where the subject title and department code match between the two datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3393\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3398\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the same term as a TIP detail record with material status 'RQ', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, and the rank of each record within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, along with the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key, where the subject, term, and offer department name match in both cases. List the columns in the following order: subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, rank, subject title (from the second subquery), subject ID, offer department name (from the second subquery), offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3311\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3632\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", show the subject title, subject key, offer department name, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, subject ID, academic year, term description, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row, ordered by offer department name and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4650\", \"desc\": \"For each degree-granting department that offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021 and has more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the total number of tip materials, the average number of enrolled students per subject (rounded to two decimal places), and the ratio of total enrolled students to total tip materials (rounded to two decimal places), listing the results in descending order of the average number of enrolled students per subject.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3493\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3868\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering where the total number of students enrolled in courses offered by that department is greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and the total enrollment is greater than 50), show the department name and total enrollment, and for each such department, show the library reserve material details with material status key equal to 'U', including the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, as well as the responsible faculty name and the offer department name, for materials offered by that department. The columns should be: department name, total enrollment, library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, subject title, windowed minimum tip material status key, responsible faculty name, and offer department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3727\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, or for each department that offered more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of tip materials. List the department code, department name, department full name, number of subjects offered, total number of enrolled students, and total number of tip materials in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3911\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1689\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school name and the highest average number of enrolled students per department (among its degree-granting departments, excluding Chemistry, and only considering subjects with at least one enrolled student), and for each subject offered by the Chemistry department in the 2019FA term that has course materials, what is the subject title, the dense rank of the subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students descending, the full name of the offering department, and the school name of the Chemistry department? List the school name and highest average enrolled students per department first, followed by the Chemistry subject title, dense rank, department full name, and Chemistry school name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3356\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), and the count of reserved materials? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and the count of reserved materials, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4287\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key equal to 'U' and for subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA', show the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title from the subject offered table, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students (only including those where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average across all subjects), the offering department name, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, the offering school name, and the responsible faculty name for each subject. Order the results by offering department and descending number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3224\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects from the term \\\"2010FA\\\" and all subjects offered in the term with code \\\"2025FA\\\", showing for each row: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank of the subject within each academic year group ordered by subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the source term (\\\"2010FA\\\" or \\\"2025FA\\\"). The columns should appear in the following order: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, minimum enrolled students per department, and source term. Order the results by subject ID and source term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4305\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4911\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with the highest maximum enrolled students (considering the current and next 2 rows ordered by subject key), display each subject's title, total units, department full name, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the department that offered the subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2461\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) with the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject ID, and the department most represented among the responsible faculty for these subjects along with the count of subjects from that department. For each such subject, also provide the corresponding academic term parameter, the term description, the average total units, and the variance of total units of all subjects offered in the corresponding effective term, considering only subjects that are offered this year and are in the Mathematics department. The columns should be: subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, maximum number of enrolled students, most prominent responsible faculty department, count of subjects from that department, academic term parameter, term description, average total units, and variance of total units. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4527\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with a non-null subject code description), and, for each subject in 2021 offered by these departments in the School of Engineering, list the subject id, subject title, and the number of enrolled students, but only include subjects where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average enrollment for that department in 2021. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3901\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4566\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that also has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', show the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the rank of each subject within its offering department, the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, the reserve catalog key, the dense rank over the material status key, and the academic year description, ordered by subject offered key and course number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3237\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4756\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1954\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2019FA' with more than 0 enrolled students, offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5), and only including courses that have course materials, show the subject title, offering department name, school name, department full name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department name. Additionally, for the same department, provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of unique subject codes associated with its courses that are offered by degree-granting departments, but only include departments other than 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each of these departments, show the total number of courses offered by the department in the '2019FA' term that have at least one enrolled student and have course materials. Present the subject title, offering department name, school name, department full name, windowed minimum enrolled students, department name, average number of unique subject codes, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of unique subject codes, and the total number of such courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1474\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 degree-granting departments (excluding 'Political Science' and Course 17) that have offered at least one subject in the 'Engineering' school, list the department name, school name, subject code description, the total number of subjects they offered, and the average number of enrolled students per subject, and for each such department, show the full names, email addresses, student years, department full names, course descriptions, course levels, the minimum course level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's last name, and the corresponding subject code and subject code description for each course taken by students named 'Kevin' in 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' (Course 6). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3736\", \"desc\": \"For each subject that both has a material status key of 'RQ' and also has an activity with enrollment type \\\"Advance sign-up required\\\" and a maximum enrollment of 12, show the subject title, the number of enrolled students from the RQ group, the term code from the library reserve material detail, the offer department name, the responsible faculty name, the tip material key, the row number within each tip material status key group ordered by subject title, the activity title, the term code from the IAP subject detail, the maximum enrollment, the term description, the term start date, the number of enrolled students from the IAP group, and the row number within each subject title group ordered by activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2181\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) that has course materials, show the subject title, term code, offering department name, responsible faculty name, department full name, school name, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject offered key, along with the minimum academic year and average total units for the corresponding academic term in the Mathematics department, where the academic year is between 2000 and 2020 or the total units are at least 6, and the total units are between 1 and 12. Also, include the term description and the first day of classes for each term from the academic terms table. The results are ordered by term code and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2398\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3277\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4640\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term '2017JA', what is the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code, the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with at least one enrolled student), and the department's school code? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4738\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\", show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, term description, and the rank of the subject within its offering department. For each tip detail record where the material status key is 'RQ', show the subject ID, term description, term start date, tip material key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the financial aid year. Additionally, for each subject offered in \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\", include the academic year description from the academic terms table. Indicate the source of each row as either 'SubjectOffered' or 'TipDetail'. The results should be ordered by subject ID and source. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3635\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3436\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects with at least 5 enrolled students, showing the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, and the row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, as well as all IAP subject activities with a maximum enrollment of 12, showing the subject ID, activity title, enrollment type, term description, and the rank of each record within each term description group ordered by activity title. Indicate the source of each record as either 'LibrarySubject' or 'IAPActivity'. The columns should be: subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, window column, activity title, enrollment type, term description, and source. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4448\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the department name, the highest total units among its subjects with exactly 12 units in the Fall Term 2024-2025, and for each course in that department that was offered in 2022 and has at least one required or optional textbook and has total units greater than the average for such courses, show the course's subject code, subject number, subject title, the term description, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number within the department ordered by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1165\", \"desc\": \"For each subject where the responsible faculty MIT ID in the library subject offered table is 928034000 or the number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table is greater than 5, and where the offer department name in the tip subject offered table is either 'Chemistry' or 'Biology', show the subject title from the library subject offered table, the offer department name from the tip subject offered table, the term code from both tables, the number of enrolled students from both tables, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table over each master subject ID group. Additionally, for the department offering the subject, show the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department. Present the results ordered by subject title and department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3236\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering that are also offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, total units, department full name, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name for the term, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, ordered by subject title and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5103\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4130\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012 that also have a section ID of 0 and a cluster type of 'S', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the total number of subjects offered by each department in that year, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the department name from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, the term start date from ACADEMIC_TERMS, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED. List the results in order by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3660\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" by the same department, show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, and the rank of each subject within its offering department ordered by subject offered key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3985\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' in departments that offer more than 5 subjects in that term, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group, and the total number of subjects per department for that term. Additionally, for each subject offered by the same department in the term '2017JA', show the number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, and whether the number of enrolled students is 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% greater than the average for that subject code), 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% less than the average for that subject code), or 'AVERAGE'. Present the results ordered by subject ID and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4197\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with term code '2012SU' that also has a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, the difference between the number of enrolled students for that subject and the average number of enrolled students for all subjects in the same department in that term, the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students, and the deviation of the number of enrolled students from the average number of enrolled students for that department in that term as calculated from the summary table. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, deviation from department average (from the first calculation), window column (dense rank), and deviation from department average (from the summary calculation). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3684\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA' by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, ordered by offering department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_93399057eb784ce69ebf1385",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 50, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject category lookup table with category name and description. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced course catalog table: an alternative catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags, section flags, meeting time/place), plus subject-offering reference columns (SO_SUBJECT_ID, SO_TERM_CODE, SO_TERM_DESCRIPTION, SO_CLUSTER_TYPE) linking catalog records to registrar subject offerings.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLABLE\", \"desc\": \"11 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_FACULTY_ROSTER\", \"desc\": \"HR faculty roster table: one row per faculty member keyed by MIT_ID with name components, terminal degree, appointment type, job/position titles across HR, administrative, and directory organization units, endowed chair, and emeritus status. Used for faculty appointment and credential analysis; joins to EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MIT_ID for contact details.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"Subject attribute lookup table decoding attribute codes attached to subjects: academic attributes (type 'A') such as calculus/science prerequisites and HASS-D/HASS category codes, and non-academic program flags (type 'N') such as ROTC, ESG, Concourse, co-op, and listener rules. Provides short, full, and reporting descriptions per code. Overlaps with CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE on HASS-family codes (HD1-HD5, HDL, HE, HA, HH, HS) but differs in scope: SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE covers all subject attribute types with one description variant per code, while CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE covers only HASS attribute codes with separate registration-form and bulletin descriptions plus attribute-group (H/G) classification. Catalog subject records' GIR_ATTRIBUTE codes all resolve against SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject person table: one row per person associated with an IAP activity, recording the person's role in the activity (Activity leader, Session leader, Contact person), MIT affiliation type, name, location, email, organization, and title. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON_KEY; used to analyze activity leadership and person roles, e.g. enrollment capacity statistics per person role.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_IAP_SCHEDULE\", \"desc\": \"10 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Library reserve material detail bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, course instructors, and material status per term. Used to count reserved materials per subject and to filter by library material status (e.g. 'U').\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\", \"desc\": \"Library course instructor table recording instructors of courses with library reserve materials, including course name, instructor name, department (in 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' format), assignment date range, and library organizational unit/branch. Referenced by LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY; instructor names resolve to person records via INSTRUCTOR_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEGREE_PROGRAM\", \"desc\": \"19 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_GROUPING\", \"desc\": \"7 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject sponsor table listing sponsors of IAP activities with sponsor name and type. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"OPA_PERSON_CURRENT\", \"desc\": \"Current-person snapshot table from the OPA (Office of People Analytics) feed: one row per current person keyed by MIT_ID with name components, email, HR job attributes (job id/title, admin employee type, HR department, org unit and position titles, payroll rank), faculty flag, employment percent, privacy flags, sabbatical begin/end dates, and personnel subarea. Used for HR/appointment analysis of current people; carries no office phone or office location.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SELECTOR\", \"desc\": \"16 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Independent Activities Period (IAP) subject detail table: one row per IAP activity offered in a January term, with activity title/description, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, fee, prerequisites, preregistration deadline, cancellation and multiple-session flags, and foreign keys to category, sponsor, session, and person tables.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SESSION\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject session table: session-level details of IAP activities including session title, description, location, date, start/end times, and sequence. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SESSION_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"CIS lookup table decoding HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute codes used in course catalog subject records. Each code (e.g. 'HA', 'HH', 'HS', 'HE', 'HD1'-'HD5', 'HDL', and combined codes like 'HA,HH') maps to two description variants: the description shown on the registration form and the shorter description printed in the bulletin, plus the CIS attribute group ('H' = HASS_ATTRIBUTE for students entering Fall 2010 or later, 'G' = GIR_ATTRIBUTE for students entering prior to Fall 2010) with a group note, and icon display attributes. Catalog tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG) join to this lookup via HASS_ATTRIBUTE. Note: a code can appear once per attribute group (e.g. 'HE' exists in both group H and group G), so joins on HASS_ATTRIBUTE alone may produce multiple matching rows.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_HOLIDAY_CLOSING_CALENDAR\", \"desc\": \"4 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room snapshot table with the same room inventory structure as FCLT_ROOMS (building/floor keys, room identifiers, major/minor use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_ROOM_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_BUILDING, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as an alternative room source when FAC_* family keys are involved.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\", \"desc\": \"Term parameter reference table holding exactly three rows that identify the SIS current term, previous term, and upcoming term, each with its term code, description, start/end dates and the last day before the next term. Used to resolve relative term references ('C', 'P', 'F') to concrete term codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building snapshot table: one row per building per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201906, 48 periods, ~255 buildings), preserving each building's attributes over time: identifiers and names, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, site, campus sector, access level, building type, ownership type, use, occupancy class, height, cost center/collector references, coordinates, and number of rooms. Used for fiscal-period building history analysis (area/room-count trends, dispersion statistics across historical records); use FCLT_BUILDING for the current snapshot. Date columns (DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED) are stored in MM/DD/YYYY format; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 is the variant storing them in DD-MON-YY format.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per physical building with the same building attribute structure as FCLT_BUILDING (number/name, type, ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates, site, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as the building dimension when FAC_* family keys are involved; FCLT_BUILDING is the counterpart in the FCLT_* family.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FCLT family): one row per major use code (e.g. CLASSRMS classrooms, OFFICES offices, LABS laboratories, RESIDENT residential) with its short code, description, and assignable-space flag. Joined from FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY to decode a room's major use; current snapshot only, use FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST for fiscal-period historical variants.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Phase 1 identified key candidates. Let me get details on the most relevant metrics (dw_2181 matches this question shape almost exactly) and tables.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_5ad75de84fdb4424b35e0929",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "semantic_get",
            "arguments": "{\"entity_ids\": \n[\"dw_2181\", \"dw_1954\", \"dw_2461\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\"]\n\n}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_5ad75de84fdb4424b35e0929",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per Chemistry subject with materials per term\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) that has course materials, show the subject title, term code, offering department name, responsible faculty name, department full name, school name, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject offered key, along with the minimum academic year and average total units for the corresponding academic term in the Mathematics department, where the academic year is between 2000 and 2020 or the total units are at least 6, and the total units are between 1 and 12. Also, include the term description and the first day of classes for each term from the academic terms table. The results are ordered by term code and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_2181\", \"name\": \"Chemistry Subjects with Course Materials 3-Row Max Enrollment vs Math Term Unit Statistics\", \"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte AS ( WITH MathTermStats AS ( SELECT s.TERM_CODE, MIN(a.ACADEMIC_YEAR) AS min_academic_year, AVG(s.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units FROM SUBJECT_SUMMARY s JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL a ON s.TERM_CODE = a.TERM_CODE WHERE s.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND s.TOTAL_UNITS BETWEEN 1 AND 12 AND ( a.ACADEMIC_YEAR BETWEEN 2000 AND 2020 OR s.TOTAL_UNITS >= 6 ) GROUP BY s.TERM_CODE ORDER BY s.TERM_CODE ), ChemistrySubjectStats AS ( SELECT t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.TERM_CODE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t0.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, t1.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, t1.SCHOOL_NAME, MAX(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER ( ORDER BY t0.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY ROWS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND 2 FOLLOWING ) AS max_num_enrolled_students FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT t1 ON t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 0 AND t0.TERM_CODE IS NOT NULL AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND t0.IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL = 'N' ) SELECT css.SUBJECT_TITLE, css.TERM_CODE, css.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, css.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, css.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, css.SCHOOL_NAME, css.max_num_enrolled_students, mts.min_academic_year, mts.avg_total_units FROM ChemistrySubjectStats css JOIN MathTermStats mts ON css.TERM_CODE = mts.TERM_CODE ) SELECT ic.SUBJECT_TITLE, ic.TERM_CODE, ic.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, ic.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, ic.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, ic.SCHOOL_NAME, ic.max_num_enrolled_students, ic.min_academic_year, ic.avg_total_units, at.TERM_DESCRIPTION, at.FIRST_DAY_OF_CLASSES FROM inner_cte ic JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON ic.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE ORDER BY ic.TERM_CODE, ic.SUBJECT_TITLE\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1954\", \"name\": \"2019FA Chemistry TIP Subjects Windowed Min Enrollment with Department Subject Code Statistics\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2019FA' with more than 0 enrolled students, offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5), and only including courses that have course materials, show the subject title, offering department name, school name, department full name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department name. Additionally, for the same department, provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of unique subject codes associated with its courses that are offered by degree-granting departments, but only include departments other than 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each of these departments, show the total number of courses offered by the department in the '2019FA' term that have at least one enrolled student and have course materials. Present the subject title, offering department name, school name, department full name, windowed minimum enrolled students, department name, average number of unique subject codes, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of unique subject codes, and the total number of such courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t0.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, t1.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, MIN(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (ORDER BY t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column, t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT t1 ON t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT t2 ON t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t2.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2019FA' AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND t0.IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL = 'N' ), course_counts AS ( SELECT t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE, COUNT(DISTINCT t0.MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER) AS total_courses FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT t1 ON t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2019FA' AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND t0.IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL = 'N' GROUP BY t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE ), subject_code_stats AS ( SELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(subj_count) AS avg_subject_codes, STDDEV(subj_count) AS stddev_subject_codes, d.DEPARTMENT_CODE FROM ( SELECT cd.DEPARTMENT, COUNT(DISTINCT sc.SUBJECT_CODE) AS subj_count FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION cd JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON cd.DEPARTMENT = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE sc ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sc.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND d.DEPARTMENT_NAME != 'Mathematics' GROUP BY cd.COURSE, cd.DEPARTMENT ) course_subjects JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON course_subjects.DEPARTMENT = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.DEPARTMENT_CODE != '18' GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, d.DEPARTMENT_CODE ) SELECT icte.SUBJECT_TITLE, icte.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, icte.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, icte.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, icte.window_column, scs.DEPARTMENT_NAME, scs.avg_subject_codes, scs.stddev_subject_codes, cc.total_courses FROM inner_cte icte JOIN subject_code_stats scs ON icte.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scs.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN course_counts cc ON icte.DEPARTMENT_CODE = cc.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY icte.SUBJECT_TITLE, scs.avg_subject_codes DESC\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per 2019FA Chemistry TIP subject with course materials matched with department-level subject code statistics\"}, {\"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per top-enrolled Chemistry subject\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) with the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject ID, and the department most represented among the responsible faculty for these subjects along with the count of subjects from that department. For each such subject, also provide the corresponding academic term parameter, the term description, the average total units, and the variance of total units of all subjects offered in the corresponding effective term, considering only subjects that are offered this year and are in the Mathematics department. The columns should be: subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, maximum number of enrolled students, most prominent responsible faculty department, count of subjects from that department, academic term parameter, term description, average total units, and variance of total units. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_2461\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Chemistry Subjects by Enrollment with Prominent Faculty Department and Math Term Unit Statistics\", \"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t0.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, t1.TERM_CODE, t1.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, MAX(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (ORDER BY t0.SUBJECT_ID ROWS BETWEEN CURRENT ROW AND 2 FOLLOWING) as max_enrolled_students, t0.SUBJECT_ID, t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN TIP_DETAIL t1 ON t0.SUBJECT_ID = t1.SUBJECT_ID WHERE t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 0 AND t1.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY IS NOT NULL AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' ), faculty_dept_counts AS ( SELECT icte.SUBJECT_TITLE, icte.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, icte.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, icte.TERM_CODE, icte.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, icte.max_enrolled_students, ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME AS Most_Prominent_Responsible_Faculty_Department, COUNT(*) AS Subject_Count FROM inner_cte icte JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso ON icte.SUBJECT_ID = ccso.SUBJECT_ID GROUP BY icte.SUBJECT_TITLE, icte.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, icte.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, icte.TERM_CODE, icte.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, icte.max_enrolled_students, ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME ), ranked_faculty_dept AS ( SELECT fdc.*, @rank := IF(@current_subject = fdc.SUBJECT_TITLE, @rank + 1, 1) AS `Rank`, @current_subject := fdc.SUBJECT_TITLE FROM (SELECT * FROM faculty_dept_counts ORDER BY SUBJECT_TITLE, Subject_Count DESC) fdc CROSS JOIN (SELECT @rank := 0, @current_subject := '') vars ), AcademicTermStats AS ( SELECT atp.TERM_CODE AS academic_term_parameter, atp.TERM_DESCRIPTION, AVG(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units, VARIANCE(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS var_total_units FROM ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER atp JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON atp.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso ON at.TERM_CODE = ccso.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE WHERE ccso.IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y' AND ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY atp.TERM_CODE, atp.TERM_DESCRIPTION ORDER BY atp.TERM_CODE ) SELECT rfd.SUBJECT_TITLE, rfd.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, rfd.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, rfd.TERM_CODE, rfd.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, rfd.max_enrolled_students, rfd.Most_Prominent_Responsible_Faculty_Department, rfd.Subject_Count, ats.academic_term_parameter, ats.TERM_DESCRIPTION, ats.avg_total_units, ats.var_total_units FROM ranked_faculty_dept rfd JOIN AcademicTermStats ats ON rfd.TERM_CODE = ats.academic_term_parameter WHERE rfd.`Rank` = 1 ORDER BY rfd.max_enrolled_students DESC LIMIT 10;\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"columns\": {\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the TIP subject offered record; joins to TIP_DETAIL.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject has no course material; 'N' means the subject has course materials\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the master subject\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master course number\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Description of the master course number\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier for clustered subjects\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master subject identifier\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the subject\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the course number\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Course number description\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '5.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the subject identifier\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject title\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_D